<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech utility Zapadoceska H1 profit down.</title>
<headline>Czech utility Zapadoceska H1 profit down.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results for six months ending June 30, 1997, according to Czech accounting standards (in millions of crowns):</p>
<p> Gross profit		   210     vs	 300</p>
<p> Operating profit	     215     vs	 300</p>
<p> Write-offs		     142     vs	 105</p>
<p>Sales of own goods</p>
<p> and services		 2,751     vs     2,757</p>
<p> Basic capital		1,606     vs     1,606</p>
<p> Total assets		 6,081     vs     5,860</p>
<p>NOTE. Full company name is Zapadoceska Energetika a.s. . The firm is a regional power distributor in the western Czech Republic. It is majority-owned by the Czech government, which has said it would soon start privatising its stakes in utilities.</p>
<p>The firm's shares are traded on the main market of the Prague Stock Exchange. Results were provided directly by the company.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
